briefs.avoids:
The subway map: rails go only where there is an order. The month keeps one strip, lit from today to the next plan only, and the week rails are gone. The navy 'UI kit' plates become graphite. The cramped tube becomes the hero, stood on the rail as the line's lit head. The stub of a lit run reaches the second stop. The setup board that pushed To do below the fold becomes one line. Amber outlines become one lamp and words. The invented '19:56' times are gone. Ideas, plain, gets its line from home. Status's bare $0.00 block becomes an instrument whose needle never rests at a bare zero. The afterglow, invisible for five rounds, becomes a steel wash and a lit edge you can see. 'Mount St. / Helens' no longer breaks, the phone no longer cuts the rail off under the fold, and the bar gets a Home item.

To make room it gives up:
- the per-week rails and their lamps on the month;
- the three-column setup board with its descriptive clauses (step 1's stays in full, steps 2 and 3 as short words);
- the tube as plate one of equal height;
- the plates' navy fill and cyan caps;
- the $0.00 block on Status (its figure moves into the meter's corner).
